<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>OrderTrack — Lookup</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/lab.css">
</head>
<body data-theme="injection">
<div class="lab-topbar"><a class="lab-back" href="/challenges">&larr; ZeroDay Academy</a><span class="name">OrderTrack</span><span class="tag">/labs/sqli-blind-boolean</span></div>
<div class="lab-wrap">
  <div class="lab-card">
    <h1>Order Lookup</h1>
    <p>Enter your order ID to check its status. The page only reveals whether a row exists.</p>
    <form method="POST" action="/labs/sqli-blind-boolean/lookup">
      <label>Order ID</label>
      <input name="id" value="<%= id %>" placeholder="e.g. 1001" autocomplete="off">
      <button type="submit">Look up</button>
    </form>
    <% if (error) { %><div class="lab-alert error"><%= error %></div><% } %>
    <% if (found !== null) { %>
      <div class="lab-alert <%= found ? 'success' : 'info' %>"><%= found ? 'Order found.' : 'No order found with that ID.' %></div>
    <% } %>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-card">
    <h2>Blind extraction</h2>
    <p>The numeric <code>id</code> is concatenated into <code>SELECT id FROM sqli_orders WHERE id = &lt;input&gt; AND customer = 'guest'</code>. Use a boolean predicate against <code>sqli_secrets</code>, extract the <code>blind-flag</code> one character at a time, then submit the flag from the challenge page.</p>
    <pre class="lab-code">1 AND (SELECT unicode(substr(value,1,1)) FROM sqli_secrets WHERE label='blind-flag') &gt; 77 --</pre>
  </div>

  <form method="POST" action="/labs/sqli-blind-boolean/reset"><button type="submit" class="secondary">Reset lab</button></form>
</div>
</body>
</html>
